    "created_at": "2018-12-10T10:03:09Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-12-10T10:03:09Z",
    "body": "I appreciate that we're standardizing this, but I'd like the layering to be different I think. I think the model should be that a style sheet also has a quirks mode slot, which it typically inherits from a document, but not always.\r\n\r\nNote that you can also end up in this situation with the `Link` header in some browsers, coupled with `document.open()`.",
